# clang-tidy for src/ and apps/ (scripts/tidy.sh; step in scripts/check.sh and CI). Counts below are warnings in
# OUR code (src/, apps/) from the first full run, 2026-11-27 (out/checks/clang-tidy-20261127.log), not tests.
#
# Two-level ratchet. Fail at once (WarningsAsErrors): every bugprone-* and performance-* check except the ones that still have findings
# (those stay plain warnings, counted below; fix a check, then delete it from the exclusions so it cannot come
# back) plus clang-analyzer-*. The rest are counted per check in scripts/tidy_baseline.json (scripts/tidy_counts.py): a count may fall, never rise.
#
# Disabled on purpose (project style, not defects):
#   readability-braces-around-statements (1600): one-line braceless ifs are the house style (.clang-format keeps them).
#   modernize-use-designated-initializers (239): positional aggregate init is used throughout (and is C++20-only churn).
#   modernize-avoid-c-arrays (92): constexpr tables, GLSL push-constant blocks and Vulkan APIs want plain arrays.
#   modernize-use-trailing-return-type, modernize-use-nodiscard: noise.
#   bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters: noise (x, y, z and dimension lists).
#   bugprone-exception-escape: the solver is built to terminate on error.
#   clang-analyzer-optin.performance.Padding: an opt-in layout hint (the UI class reports 151 padding bytes), not a defect.
# Analyzer findings in the baseline (look at these): core.NonNullParamChecker src/app/farm_client.cpp:807,
#   unix.StdCLibraryFunctions apps/emfdtd/main.cpp:253 (fdopen with fd < 0), security.FloatLoopCounter (an alias of
#   bugprone-float-loop-counter).
# Still warnings (counts in our code): bugprone-signed-bitwise 163, bugprone-narrowing-conversions 40,
#   performance-inefficient-vector-operation 22, performance-enum-size 18, bugprone-unchecked-string-to-number-
#   conversion 16, performance-inefficient-string-concatenation 10, bugprone-float-loop-counter 7,
#   bugprone-invalid-enum-default-initialization 6, bugprone-incorrect-roundings 5,
#   bugprone-implicit-widening-of-multiplication-result 5, bugprone-empty-catch 5, performance-use-std-move 2,
#   bugprone-nondeterministic-pointer-iteration-order 2, bugprone-assignment-in-if-condition 2, and one each of
#   performance-unnecessary-value-param, performance-unnecessary-copy-initialization, performance-faster-string-find,
#   performance-prefer-single-char-overloads, bugprone-unused-local-non-trivial-variable,
#   bugprone-throwing-static-initialization, bugprone-suspicious-memory-comparison, bugprone-command-processor,
#   bugprone-branch-clone. Other modernize-* findings (use-ranges 52, use-emplace 43, use-scoped-lock 42, use-auto 26,
#   ...) stay warnings and are never errors.
Checks: >
  -*,bugprone-*,performance-*,modernize-*,clang-analyzer-*,
  -readability-braces-around-statements,-modernize-use-designated-initializers,-modernize-avoid-c-arrays,
  -modernize-use-trailing-return-type,-modernize-use-nodiscard,-bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
  -bugprone-exception-escape,-clang-analyzer-optin.performance.Padding
WarningsAsErrors: >
  bugprone-*,performance-*,clang-analyzer-*,
  -bugprone-signed-bitwise,-bugprone-narrowing-conversions,-performance-inefficient-vector-operation,
  -performance-enum-size,-bugprone-unchecked-string-to-number-conversion,
  -performance-inefficient-string-concatenation,-bugprone-float-loop-counter,
  -bugprone-invalid-enum-default-initialization,-bugprone-incorrect-roundings,
  -bugprone-implicit-widening-of-multiplication-result,-bugprone-empty-catch,-performance-use-std-move,
  -bugprone-nondeterministic-pointer-iteration-order,-bugprone-assignment-in-if-condition,
  -performance-unnecessary-value-param,-performance-unnecessary-copy-initialization,
  -performance-faster-string-find,-performance-prefer-single-char-overloads,
  -bugprone-unused-local-non-trivial-variable,-bugprone-throwing-static-initialization,
  -bugprone-suspicious-memory-comparison,-bugprone-command-processor,-bugprone-branch-clone,
  -clang-analyzer-security.FloatLoopCounter,-clang-analyzer-core.NonNullParamChecker,
  -clang-analyzer-unix.StdCLibraryFunctions
# Header filter: set by scripts/tidy.sh from the checkout's root (not from its folder name), and proven by the canary.
